  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): セイヨウノダイコン",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%A8%E3%82%A6%E3%83%8E%E3%83%80%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B3%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 106365370,
      "text": "セイヨウノダイコン は、アブラナ科の被子植物の一つである。食用のダイコン Raphanus sativus の祖先と主張されることがある。アジア（あるいは一部の権威によれば地中海）原産で、世界のほとんどの地域に帰化しており、多くの地域（例えばオーストラリア）において有害な侵入種と見なされている。素早く広がり、道端などでしばしば見られる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Raphanus raphanistrum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1372180236,
      "text": "Raphanus raphanistrum, also known as wild radish, white charlock or jointed charlock, is a flowering plant in the family Brassicaceae. The species is native to western Asia, Europe and parts of Northern Africa. It has been introduced into most parts of the world and is regarded as a habitat threatening invasive species in many areas, for example, Australia. It spreads rapidly and is often found growing on roadsides or in other places where the ground has been disturbed. The cultivated radish, widely used as a root vegetable, is sometimes considered to be one of its subspecies as Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Raphanus raphanistrum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 171665659,
      "text": "La rabaniza, rabizón o rábano silvestre es una planta herbácea anual de la familia de las brasicáceas. Se la considera una de las posibles antepasadas del rábano doméstico."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Raphanus raphanistrum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 235900829,
      "text": "La Ravenelle, Radis ravenelle ou Radis sauvage (Raphanus raphanistrum), est une espèce de plantes annuelles communes de la famille des Brassicaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Raphanus raphanistrum",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 67981826,
      "text": "Raphanus raphanistrum é uma espécie de planta com flor pertencente à família Brassicaceae com os nomes comuns de labrestos, saramago, ineixa, rapistro, rábano-bastardo e rábano-silvestre."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Raphanus raphanistrum",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 29960440,
      "text": "Raphanus raphanistrum adalah tanaman berbunga di keluarga Brassicaceae. Kadang-kadang diklaim sebagai leluhur lobak yang dapat dimakan, Raphanus sativus. Berasal dari Asia barat, Eropa dan sebagian Afrika Utara. Ini telah diperkenalkan ke sebagian besar dunia dan dianggap sebagai habitat yang mengancam spesies invasif di banyak daerah, misalnya, Australia. Ini menyebar dengan cepat dan sering ditemukan tumbuh di tepi jalan atau di tempat-tempat lain di mana tanah telah terganggu."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Raphanus raphanistrum § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1372180236,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "All tender parts of the plant are edible. The leaves and flowers have a spicy taste or aftertaste. The seedpods can be eaten, as can the outer skin of the root (after being washed). It is said that John Walker cultivated sea radish root as an alternative to horseradish after discovering the plant on the west coast of Scotland as early as 1753.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "es": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (es): Raphanus raphanistrum § Usos",
        "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum#Usos",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 171665659,
        "heading": "Usos",
        "text": "En la isla de Gran Canaria es típico de hacer el potaje de jaramago.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Raphanus raphanistrum § Utilisation",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raphanus_raphanistrum#Utilisation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 235900829,
        "heading": "Utilisation",
        "text": "C'est une source importante de pollen et de nectar pour les pollinisateurs, en particulier les abeilles au début du printemps.\nDifférentes parties de la plante sont comestibles, les feuilles et les jeunes fruits peuvent être mangés crus, cuits ou en lacto-fermentation.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
